  "title": "Spot Repeated Lies",
  "description": "Be wary of repeated statements: - Fact-check: Look up evidence for claims you’ve heard multiple times. - Question familiarity: Ask, \"Do I believe this because it’s true or just because I’ve heard it a lot?\" - Practice skepticism: Even well-designed ads or viral posts can repeat falsehoods convincingly. Example: Heard \"You need to drink 8 glasses of water a day\"? Check the science instead of relying on repetition.",
